   "locked": false
  },
  {
   "id": "e808",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1510,
   "y": 5975.0,
   "width": 715.0,
   "height": 150.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 169683137,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1099264208,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "More KV heads (small H/G)\n  -> more independent K/V representations\n  -> potentially better quality\n  -> more KV memory AND more bytes read every decode step.\nFewer KV heads (large H/G): the reverse.\nH/G must be a whole number: each KV head serves exactly H/G query heads\n(32 Q, 8 KV -> 'sharing ratio 4': 4 Q heads -> 1 KV head).\nEvery row is far below the A100 ridge (~200 FLOP/B): decode stays memory-bound.",
   "originalText": "More KV heads (small H/G)\n  -> more independent K/V representations\n  -> potentially better quality\n  -> more KV memory AND more bytes read every decode step.\nFewer KV heads (large H/G): the reverse.\nH/G must be a whole number: each KV head serves exactly H/G query heads\n(32 Q, 8 KV -> 'sharing ratio 4': 4 Q heads -> 1 KV head).\nEvery row is far below the A100 ridge (~200 FLOP/B): decode stays memory-bound.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "e807",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
